# Subnormal two-perfect signalizers

A.4.2(2)–(7) and A.4.3 are proved by the imported modules. A subnormal
chain identifies the residual of a permutable supplement; commutators
then place signalizers in the actual section centralizer, whose Sylow
two-subgroups are precisely the maximal signalizers. Sylow intersections,
normalizer arguments, and conjugacy give the core and normal-closure
conclusions. Both core-product equalities are retained in A.4.3.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*,
Appendix A.4, printed pp. 56–58.
-/
